    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Since the increase in power with sample size results from a reduction in the sampling variance, it is again useful to write the sampling variance of $ b_{op} $ as some function $ f $ divided by the number $ N $ of families, $ \\sigma^2(b_{op}) = f_{op}^2 / N $. From Equation 17.6",
      "source_page": 886,
      "printed_page": 866,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p068:b4"
      ],
