    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This expression, which assumes single parents and single offspring, can easily be modified to account for midparents and/or multiple offspring per family. With $n$ measured offspring per family, $\\sigma^{2}(z_{\\bar{o}}) = \\sigma^{2}(z_{o})[t + (1 - t)/n]$ replaces $\\sigma^{2}(z_{o})$, where $t$ is the correlation between full sibs. Likewise, for a midparent-offspring regression, $\\sigma^{2}(z_{\\bar{p}}) = \\sigma^{2}(z_{p})/2$ replaces $\\sigma^{2}(z_{p})$, and $r_{o\\bar{p}}$ and $b_{o\\bar{p}}$ replace $r_{op}$ and $b_{op}$. Chapter 17 discusses these modifications in more detail",
      "source_page": 886,
      "printed_page": 866,
      "source_block_ids": [
